e. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-257-weighted"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-257-weighted"],"id":"long.thm-257-weighted","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 1.1 (A weighted summability criterion)","locator":"Long record Theorem 1.1, p. 8, label thm:257-weighted","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $b\\ge2$ be an integer, let $\\mathcal P$ be a finite nonempty set of primes, and let $A\\subseteq\\mathbb N_{>0}$ be infinite. Write\n$$\nh(a)=\\prod_{p\\in\\mathcal P}p^{v_p(a)},\n$$\nwhere $v_p(a)$ is the exponent of $p$ in $a$; thus $h(a)$ is the $\\mathcal P$-part of $a$. If\n$$\n\n\n W_{b,\\mathcal P}(A):=\n \\sum_{a\\in A}\\frac{h(a)}{a\\bigl(b^{h(a)}-1\\bigr)}<\\infty,\n$$\nthen\n$$\nX_A(b)=\\sum_{a\\in A}\\frac1{b^a-1}\n$$\nis irrational. More precisely, for\n$$\n\\Delta_{b,A}(m)=\n \\sum_{a\\in A}\\frac{b^{m\\bmod a}-1}{b^a-1},\n$$\nfor every $\\varepsilon>0$ and every $N$ there is an $m\\ge N$ with $0<\\Delta_{b,A}(m)<\\varepsilon$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.thm-257-weighted","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.thm-257-weighted","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.thm-257-weighted%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR7.DivisibilityWeightedClaim%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.thm-257-weighted%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR7.DivisibilityWeightedClaim%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR7.DivisibilityWeightedClaim"},{"